Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The previous strategy achieved perfect syntax but very low task accuracy
// because it still behaved like a token-level syntax maintainer rather than a
// query finisher. The observed outputs such as short SQL prefixes indicate that
// the policy was willing to close or stall as soon as a locally valid fragment
// existed, without pushing toward the larger structural milestones of Spider
// queries: FROM clauses, joins, predicates, grouping, ordering, and so on.
//
// This revision changes the constrained policy from "sample among valid tokens"
// to "advance by parser symbols whenever possible". Inside a constrained SQL
// span, we no longer do custom logit boosting and one-token fallback logic.
// Instead, we use ConstrainedSymbol with the provided stepTokenBudget. That
// helper is designed to spend several LM calls to complete one parser-approved
// symbol of the grammar, which is much better matched to SQL generation than
// raw token-by-token steering. This directly targets the short-prefix failure:
// each successful constrained iteration now tends to add a meaningful valid SQL
// unit rather than merely preserving validity one token at a time.
//
// We also make completion behavior more decisive. While inside the constrained
// span, if the parser says the SQL prefix is complete, we immediately emit the
// closing delimiter with CloseConstrainedSpan and stop the constrained region.
// We never close merely because a sampled token looks like ">>"; closure only
// happens from a parser-complete state, preserving the intended semantics.
//
// Outside the constrained span, we keep a simple one-token policy using
// UnconstrainedStep so that the answer reliably contains the required << >>
// delimiters. Once the span is opened, generation stays grammar-driven until
// completion, EOS, or budget exhaustion. This removes the earlier rollback-heavy
// behavior that often terminated without making semantic progress.
//
// Finally, returned cost is now tied to the local steps counter in a way that
// mirrors the helper contracts: one step for each UnconstrainedStep or
// CloseConstrainedSpan, and stepsUsed for each ConstrainedSymbol call. This
// yields a cleaner progress argument and a strategy that spends its budget on
// constructing a full valid SQL query instead of repeatedly reconsidering the
// same short prefix.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the outside-span branch, UnconstrainedStep either keeps us
// outside the constrained region or opens it with currentConstrainedOut := [];
// since parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by precondition, the invariant is
// preserved. In the complete-prefix branch, CloseConstrainedSpan exits the
// constrained region, so the implication becomes vacuous. In the
// ConstrainedSymbol branch, the helper returns a currentOut that remains a valid
// parser prefix when we stay inside; if EOS is hit we break immediately.
//
// suffix: While outside the span, currentConstrainedOut is [], so the suffix
// invariant is trivial; if we open a span, the tracked constrained content is
// still empty and therefore matches the empty suffix of generated. In the close
// branch, we leave the constrained region and reset currentConstrainedOut to [],
// so the implication is vacuous. In the ConstrainedSymbol branch, the helper
// extends the constrained content and generated consistently by the returned
// symbol, so generated still ends with currentConstrainedOut.
//
// progress: UnconstrainedStep appends exactly 1 token and we increment steps by
// 1. CloseConstrainedSpan appends exactly 1 token and we increment steps by 1.
// ConstrainedSymbol appends stepsUsed tokens to the constrained region and we
// increment steps by stepsUsed. Any branch that does not continue generation
// breaks immediately. Therefore |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is
// preserved by linear arithmetic.
//
// cost_accounting: The loop maintains 0 <= steps <= maxSteps. Each continuing
// branch increases steps by exactly the amount of generation work performed:
// 1 for UnconstrainedStep and CloseConstrainedSpan, and stepsUsed for
// ConstrainedSymbol. Break branches do not change steps. Thus assigning
// cost := steps at the end proves cost <= maxSteps.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps := 0;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  invariant cost == 0
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    var next := helpers.UnconstrainedStep(lm, prompt, generated);
    if next == eosToken {
      break;
    } else {
      generated := generated + [next];
      steps := steps + 1;
      if Contains(next, "<<") {
        insideConstrainedOut := true;
        currentConstrainedOut := [];
      }
    }
  } else {
    var isComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
    if isComplete {
      if steps + 1 <= maxSteps {
        var generated2, inside2, current2 := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
        generated := generated2;
        insideConstrainedOut := inside2;
        currentConstrainedOut := current2;
        steps := steps + 1;
      } else {
        break;
      }
    } else {
      var constrainedPrompt := prompt + generated[..|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|];
      var current2, hitEos, stepsUsed := helpers.ConstrainedSymbol(
        lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, stepTokenBudget, eosToken
      );
      if hitEos {
        break;
      } else {
        if steps + stepsUsed <= maxSteps {
          generated := constrainedPrompt[|prompt|..] + current2;
          currentConstrainedOut := current2;
          insideConstrainedOut := true;
          steps := steps + stepsUsed;
        } else {
          break;
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

cost := steps;

